ction.\n\nLet me look at the DummyLM utility and how adapter passes lm_kwargs. The adapter calls `lm(messages=inputs, **lm_kwargs)`. So I can mock/patch the LM to capture kwargs.\n\nLet me check `dspy/utils/dummies.py` and existing tests that inspect lm call kwargs.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now let's verify the change and write a test. Let me check how DummyLM works to write a test that verifies:\\n1. Valid prediction dict is moved to config and removed from inputs.\\n2. Invalid prediction (e.g., string, or dict without proper type/content) stays as input.\\n3. Works with async too.\\n4. The config passed to the LM includes prediction.\\n\\nLet me look at the DummyLM utility and how adapter passes lm_kwargs. The adapter calls `lm(messages=inputs, **lm_kwargs)`. So I can mock/patch the LM to capture kwargs.\\n\\nLet me check `dspy/utils/dummies.py` and existing tests that inspect lm call kwargs.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me verify the change and check how the DummyLM test utility works so I can write tests:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cb29027ceb964b7cb3faa1d6","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":45,"offset":93,"path":"/testbed/dspy/predict/predict.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5a81f7678ea34022a9c2350b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -rn \"class DummyLM\" -A 40 /testbed/dspy/utils/dummies.py | head -60"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1263,"output":224,"cacheRead":11264,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":139,"totalTokens":12751,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788459052061,"responseId":"gen-1788459052-xy0fizdTPNPCR3odX05J","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cb29027ceb964b7cb3faa1d6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"    def _forward_preprocess(self, **kwargs):\n        # Extract the three privileged keyword arguments.\n        assert \"new_signature\" not in kwargs, \"new_signature is no longer a valid keyword argument.\"\n        signature = ensure_signature(kwargs.pop(\"signature\", self.signature))\n        demos = kwargs.pop(\"demos\", self.demos)\n        config = dict(**self.config, **kwargs.pop(\"config\", {}))\n\n        # Get the right LM to use.\n        lm = kwargs.pop(\"lm\", self.lm) or settings.lm\n        assert isinstance(lm, BaseLM), \"No LM is loaded.\"\n\n        # If temperature is unset or <=0.15, and n > 1, set temperature to 0.7 to keep randomness.\n        temperature = config.get(\"temperature\") or lm.kwargs.get(\"temperature\")\n        num_generations = config.get(\"n\") or lm.kwargs.get(\"n\") or lm.kwargs.get(\"num_generations\") or 1\n\n        if (temperature is None or temperature <= 0.15) and num_generations > 1:\n            config[\"temperature\"] = 0.7\n\n        # If the input contains a predicted output (OpenAI's Predicted Outputs\n        # feature), move it to the LM config so it can guide the generation\n        # instead of being treated as a regular input field.\n        prediction = kwargs.get(\"prediction\")\n        if isinstance(prediction, dict) and prediction.get(\"type\") == \"content\" and \"content\" in prediction:\n            kwargs.pop(\"prediction\")\n            config[\"prediction\"] = prediction\n\n        if not all(k in kwargs for k in signature.input_fields):\n            present = [k for k in signature.input_fields if k in kwargs]\n            missing = [k for k in signature.input_fields if k not in kwargs]\n            logger.warning(\n                \"Not all input fields were provided to module. Present: %s. Missing: %s.\",\n                present,\n                missing,\n            )\n        return lm, config, signature, demos, kwargs\n\n    def _forward_postprocess(self, completions, signature, **kwargs):\n        pred = Prediction.from_completions(completions, signature=signature)\n        if kwargs.pop(\"_trace\", True) and settings.trace is not None:\n            trace = settings.trace\n            trace.append((self, {**kwargs}, pred))\n        return pred\n\n    def _should_stream(self):\n        stream_listeners = settings.stream_listeners or []\n\n[66 more lines in file. Use offset=138 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788459063765},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5a81f7678ea34022a9c2350b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"14:class DummyLM(LM):\n15-    \"\"\"Dummy language model for unit testing purposes.\n16-\n17-    Three modes of operation:\n18-\n19-    Mode 1: List of dictionaries\n20-\n21-    If a list of dictionaries is provided, the dummy model will return the next dictionary\n22-    in the list for each request, formatted according to the `format_field_with_value` function.\n23-\n24-    Example:\n25-\n26-    ```\n27-    lm = DummyLM([{\"answer\": \"red\"}, {\"answer\": \"blue\"}])\n28-    dspy.settings.configure(lm=lm)\n29-    predictor(\"What color is the sky?\")\n30-    # Output:\n31-    # [[## answer ##]]\n32-    # red\n33-    predictor(\"What color is the sky?\")\n34-    # Output:\n35-    # [[## answer ##]]\n36-    # blue\n37-    ```\n38-\n39-    Mode 2: Dictionary of dictionaries\n40-\n41-    If a dictionary of dictionaries is provided, the dummy model will return the value\n42-    corresponding to the key which is contained with the final message of the prompt,\n43-    formatted according to the `format_field_with_value` function from the chat adapter.\n44-\n45-    ```\n46-    lm = DummyLM({\"What color is the sky?\": {\"answer\": \"blue\"}})\n47-    dspy.settings.configure(lm=lm)\n48-    predictor(\"What color is the sky?\")\n49-    # Output:\n50-    # [[## answer ##]]\n51-    # blue\n52-    ```\n53-\n54-    Mode 3: Follow examples\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788459063765},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The implementation looks g